    if (x > 100) [[unlikely]] {
        return x * 2;
    } 
    return x + 5;
}
```
Only use `[[likely]]` or `[[unlikely]]` if you have profiled your data and know the exact distribution, otherwise, it can actually hurt performance. Sticking to the ternary operator is usually the safest and fastest bet!

